' 05 Head-only queue: the states of one queue collection of a native space.
'
' Source of Figure N4 in ../design.md (section N4). The figure restates the
' bump of rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/counter.rs, the plans offer and
' receive of spaces/generic.rs, the head rule of spaces/disciplines/queue.rs,
' and the fire rounds of reified/costs.rs (decisions 11, 30, 31 and 43, P4
' design item A10, plan revision I-21). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. A collection starts unopened. Its first operation consumes the space
'      counter, opens the collection counter at 1, and takes the order 0.
'   2. Every later operation bumps the collection counter from v to v + 1
'      and takes the order v. A re-issued persistent operation keeps the
'      order of its first round and re-enters at its place (decision 43).
'   3. The open collection is in one of four states, by the records R and
'      the waiters W that it holds.
'   4. A send meets only the head waiter, and a receive meets only the head
'      record. A head that does not match blocks every entry behind it.
'   5. Notes give the fire rounds: the re-offer, the persistent drain, the
'      re-issue of a divergent pair, and the cap of 64 fires.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 05-head-only-queue.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 05-head-only-queue
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam StateBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title States of one queue collection (head-only matching, decision 11)

state "Unopened" as UNOPENED $rrs_reserved : no counter record on <latex>S(\mathit{sid}, k)</latex>
state "Open collection" as OPEN $ca_pkg_indigo {
  state "Empty" as EMPTY $rrs_storage : <latex>R = \emptyset,\ W = \emptyset</latex>
  state "Records queued" as RECORDS $rrs_storage : <latex>R \neq \emptyset,\ W = \emptyset</latex>
  state "Waiters queued" as WAITERS $rrs_storage : <latex>R = \emptyset,\ W \neq \emptyset</latex>
  state "Blocked" as BLOCKED $ca_note_amber : <latex>R \neq \emptyset,\ W \neq \emptyset</latex>\nthe head waiter does not match\nthe head record, so nothing fires\nno fresh operation leaves this state\na re-entry ahead of a head can fire\n(decision 43)

  [*] --> EMPTY
  EMPTY --> RECORDS : send, no waiter:\nstore the record
  EMPTY --> WAITERS : receive, no record:\npark the waiter

  RECORDS --> RECORDS : send: store at the tail\nreceive that fires with the head:\nthe head leaves, or stays for a peek\nor a persistent record
  RECORDS --> EMPTY : receive that fires\nwith the last record
  RECORDS --> BLOCKED : receive that does not\nmatch the head record:\npark the waiter
  RECORDS --> WAITERS : persistent receive <=\ndrains every record, then parks

  WAITERS --> WAITERS : receive: park at the tail\nsend that fires the head waiter:\nthe waiter leaves, or stays if persistent
  WAITERS --> EMPTY : send that fires\nthe last waiter
  WAITERS --> BLOCKED : send that does not\nmatch the head waiter:\nstore the record
  WAITERS --> RECORDS : the datum survives every fire\n(a peek waiter, or a send !!),\nthen no waiter matches: store

  BLOCKED --> BLOCKED : send: store at the tail\nreceive: park at the tail
}

[*] --> UNOPENED
UNOPENED --> OPEN : first operation: consume <latex>S(\mathit{sid})</latex> and produce it again,\nopen <latex>S(\mathit{sid}, k) = 1</latex>, take the order 0

note right of OPEN
  **Every operation** bumps <latex>S(\mathit{sid}, k)</latex>
  from <latex>v</latex> to <latex>v + 1</latex> and takes the order <latex>v</latex>,
  also a peek and a fire that changes no state
  (decision 31). Entries have distinct orders.

  **Re-entry** (decision 43): a re-issued persistent
  operation keeps the order of its first round. It is
  at the head when its side is empty or its order is
  below the order of the head. Otherwise it is stored
  or parked at its place and fires nothing.

  **Head of a side:** the least <latex>(\mathit{ord}, \mathrm{bincode})</latex>.
  A fresh send meets the head waiter only when R is empty.
  A fresh receive meets the head record only when W is empty.

  **Fire rounds** in one transaction:
  Re-offer: a peek waiter leaves the datum alive,
  and the next round offers it to the next head waiter.
  Drain: a persistent receive meets the next head record.
  Re-issue: a divergent pair (a send !! with a receive <=,
  or a receive <= with a record of !!) re-issues after
  one round, and any chain re-issues after 64 fires (I-21).

  **INV** holds at the end of every deploy:
  <latex>R = \emptyset \lor W = \emptyset \lor \neg\, \mathrm{match}(\mathrm{head}(W), \mathrm{head}(R))</latex>
  Inside a deploy, the heads can match only while a
  persistent element in flight precedes the head of its side.
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_reserved>   | not opened: the collection has no counter yet |
|<$rrs_storage>    | stored state of the collection: records, waiters, counter |
|<$ca_note_amber>  | blocked: both sides wait behind heads that do not match |
endlegend
@enduml
